{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChH74XQWFfZ4NQse2e8pZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XwaEyU5c4nBjGpNX3xVue1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.install-workflow-fixes-02-config-step-enables-plugin/README.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":71287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":393},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af2d0abd-9e83-4754-8c85-3fb46e7ec1b3","uuid":"9240fe47-149c-43a5-a289-d09a3fb06540","timestamp":"2026-11-22T01:33:22.339Z","request_id":"req_011ChH74XF5YB9Cifxr7vBfZ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XwaEyU5c4nBjGpNX3xVue1":{"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.install-workflow-fixes-02-config-step-enables-plugin/README.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XwaEyU5c4nBjGpNX3xVue1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# tiiny-router-hermes\n2\t\n3\tTiiny model routing for the Hermes harness.\n4\t\n5\tThis package chooses which model does each job.\n6\tEach specialist model gets the task's goal and context without\n7\tinheriting the manager's full conversation history.\n8\tSee\n9\t[Hermes delegation](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/delegation).\n10\t\n11\tThis installs global config, in `~/.hermes/` -- a Hermes plugin,\n12\tcontroller scripts, and a skill for delegating tasks on\n13\ta Tiiny hardware device. (Hermes loads plugins from `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/`.)\n14\t\n15\tWe are using Hermes's pluggable `DelegationProvider` to select\n16\ta model, provider, and reasoning settings for each subtask.\n17\t\n18\t\n19\t<details><summary><h2>Contents</h2></summary>\n20\t\n21\t<!-- toc -->\n22\t\n23\t- [Prerequisites](#prerequisites)\n24\t- [Install](#install)\n25\t- [What is the Hermes harness?](#what-is-the-hermes-harness)\n26\t- [Request flow](#request-flow)\n27\t- [When Tiiny routing applies](#when-tiiny-routing-applies)\n28\t- [Reducing model swaps](#reducing-model-swaps)\n29\t- [The config step](#the-config-step)\n30\t  * [Settings written by the installer](#settings-written-by-the-installer)\n31\t- [Check the install](#check-the-install)\n32\t- [Upgrade](#upgrade)\n33\t- [Uninstall](#uninstall)\n34\t- [More](#more)\n35\t\n36\t<!-- tocstop -->\n37\t\n38\t</details>\n39\t\n40\t## Prerequisites\n41\t\n42\t* [Hermes](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/) installed\n43\t* a [tiiny device](https://tiiny.ai/)\n44\t\n45\t## Install\n46\t\n47\tThe npm package is `hermes-tiiny-router`; its command is `hermesrouter`\n48\t(the install command is `npx hermesrouter install`).\n49\t\n50\t```sh\n51\tnpm i -D hermes-tiiny-router\n52\t```\n53\t\n54\tInstall the Hermes plugin, then choose whether to configure it (see\n55\t[the config step](#the-config-step)):\n56\t\n57\t```bash\n58\tnpx hermesrouter install\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\tThis copies a directory to `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`\n62\t(`HERMES_HOME` defaults to `~/.hermes`). It holds the routing backend, the\n63\tcontroller scripts and the skill, which Hermes serves as\n64\t`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`. The installer then runs\n65\t`hermes plugins validate` on the directory.\n66\t\n67\tInstalling the npm dependency alone does not install or configure the\n68\tHermes plugin. **The plugin is installed at the Hermes user level**,\n69\teven when the npm dependency is local to a project.\n70\t\n71\tAdd the device's bearer token to `~/.hermes/.env` yourself.\n72\t\n73\t```sh\n74\t# ~/.hermes/.env\n75\tTIINY_API_KEY=\"...\"\n76\t```\n77\t\n78\t## What is the Hermes harness?\n79\t\n80\t[Hermes Agent][hermes] is a harness from Nous Research. It provides the\n81\texecution loop, model-provider integration, and session storage, along\n82\twith persistent memory, reusable skills, scheduled tasks, messaging\n83\tintegrations, and subagent delegation. Its learning features include\n84\tsaving and improving skills and memories across sessions.\n85\t\n86\tThis plugin selects models for subtasks.\n87\t\n88\t## Request flow\n89\t\n90\tWith delegation configured to use Tiiny:\n91\t\n92\t```text\n93\tYour request\n94\t  -> Hermes manager agent\n95\t  -> delegate_task(goal, context)\n96\t  -> Tiiny routing backend\n97\t  -> selected model on the Tiiny device\n98\t  -> result returned to the manager\n99\t```\n100\t\n101\tHermes supplies the child agent's execution loop, tools, and isolated\n102\tconversation. This plugin selects the model, taking the task, the batch\n103\tplan, and the device's loaded models into account. See\n104\t[Hermes delegation][hermes-delegation] for how child agents run and return\n105\ttheir results.\n106\t\n107\t## When Tiiny routing applies\n108\t\n109\tThe intended scope is **Hermes delegating work to Tiiny hardware**. The\n110\tmanager can use a cloud model; it does not need to run on Tiiny. Installing\n111\tthis package does not change how other agent harnesses route tasks.\n112\t\n113\tHermes calls this router for `delegate_task` when its configuration selects\n114\t`delegation.backend: tiiny-router`. That selection persists across new\n115\tsessions using the same configuration. Changing the manager's model or\n116\tprovider does not turn the router on or off.\n117\t\n118\t**The current code does not enforce a Tiiny-only guard.** The skill tells\n119\tthe manager to use it only with Tiiny, but the backend does not validate\n120\tthe delegation provider or endpoint before choosing a Tiiny model and\n121\tcontacting the device. It copies the delegation configuration into the\n122\treturned route, then sets the model and reasoning overrides. Selecting\n123\tthis backend alone does not bind the child to the `tiiny` provider.\n124\t\n125\tThe installer adds that provider but does not set `delegation.provider`.\n126\tFor Tiiny workers, explicitly select it in the same Hermes configuration:\n127\t\n128\t```bash\n129\thermes config set delegation.provider tiiny\n130\t```\n131\t\n132\tCheck existing delegation overrides too: `delegation.base_url` takes\n133\tprecedence over the provider. Without a delegation provider or endpoint,\n134\tchildren inherit the manager's provider and credentials. An unreachable\n135\tdevice does not automatically disable this backend, and configured\n136\tfallback providers can send failed child tasks to a cloud model.\n137\t\n138\tUse a dedicated [Hermes profile][hermes-profiles] for Tiiny work, with the\n139\tbackend set to `default` in configurations used for other providers. Set\n140\t`HERMES_HOME` explicitly when installing for a profile so the package and\n141\tits `hermes` subprocesses target the same home. For example, after creating\n142\ta profile named `tiiny`:\n143\t\n144\t```bash\n145\tHERMES_HOME=\"$HOME/.hermes/profiles/tiiny\" \\\n146\t  npx hermesrouter install --configure\n147\tHERMES_HOME=\"$HOME/.hermes/profiles/tiiny\" \\\n148\t  hermes config set delegation.provider tiiny\n149\t```\n150\t\n151\tThis separates the configurations; a runtime check would still be needed\n152\tto guarantee that this backend cannot be used with a non-Tiiny route.\n153\t\n154\t## Reducing model swaps\n155\t\n156\tThe package helps avoid repeated loading and unloading in two ways:\n157\t\n158\t- **Reuse loaded models.** For each task, the router first considers its\n159\t  planned model if loaded, then loaded candidates in the task's tier,\n160\t  then the loaded generalist. Without a loaded match, it chooses the\n161\t  tier's default; if residency cannot be read, it uses the generalist\n162\t  unless a plan supplies a model. By default it calls the controller's\n163\t  `ensure_model` before returning the route. An already loaded model is\n164\t  checked and reused rather than reloaded.\n165\t- **Plan model-loading waves.** Given several goals, the controller's\n166\t  `plan` command chooses their models, collects the distinct models,\n167\t  and packs them into waves whose combined NPU share fits within 100%.\n168\t  Models already loaded are packed first. Every task assigned to a\n169\t  particular model gets that model's wave number. A wave can contain\n170\t  several models if they fit together.\n171\t\n172\tFor example, independent goals that would alternate between two models\n173\tthat cannot fit together can instead run all work for one model before\n174\tloading the other. Loading a wave keeps other resident models when there\n175\tis room and skips loading models that are already resident.\n176\t\n177\t**Grouping is planned, but execution depends on the manager following the\n178\tskill.** The router handles one task at a time; it does not maintain a\n179\tqueue or reorder arbitrary `delegate_task` calls. The installed skill\n180\tinstructs the manager to plan the batch, reserve the device, load a wave,\n181\tfinish that wave's work, then load the next. The skill also instructs the\n182\tmanager to run only one generation-heavy child at a time. After the batch,\n183\t`release` restores the controller's required models and clears the plan\n184\tand lock; restoration can itself require loading models.\n185\t\n186\tAd hoc delegation still gets model selection and on-demand loading, but\n187\tdoes not get automatic grouping across separate calls. Batching reduces\n188\tswaps when the work permits it; it does not eliminate their time cost.\n189\tSee the [routing skill](tiiny-router/SKILL.md) for the full procedure.\n190\t\n191\t## The config step\n192\t\n193\t`npx hermesrouter install` copies the plugin and validates it, then offers\n194\tto change Hermes configuration through `hermes config set`.\n195\t\n196\t```bash\n197\tnpx hermesrouter install                 # prompts in a terminal\n198\tnpx hermesrouter install --configure     # applies without asking\n199\tnpx hermesrouter install --no-configure  # installs files only\n200\t```\n201\t\n202\tWithout a terminal and without either flag, it skips configuration and\n203\tprints the commands. Declining the prompt or using `--no-configure` also\n204\tleaves settings unchanged.\n205\t\n206\tThese are persistent Hermes user settings, not settings in the npm\n207\tproject. With the default Hermes home/profile they live in\n208\t`~/.hermes/config.yaml`; a named profile has its own configuration. The\n209\tinstaller copies files to `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/` (falling\n210\tback to `~/.hermes`) and lets the invoked `hermes` command choose its\n211\tconfiguration. Use an explicit `HERMES_HOME` to keep those targets aligned\n212\twhen working with profiles.\n213\t\n214\t### Settings written by the installer\n215\t\n216\tThe config step sets `delegation.backend` to `tiiny-router` and writes the\n217\tfollowing fields under `providers.tiiny`:\n218\t\n219\t| Field | Value |\n220\t| --- | --- |\n221\t| `name` | `tiiny` |\n222\t| `api` | `http://openai.api.tiiny/v1` |\n223\t| `key_env` | `TIINY_API_KEY` |\n224\t| `transport` | `chat_completions` |\n225\t| `default_model` | `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` |\n226\t| `context_length` | `262144` |\n227\t| `models_discovered` | `false` |\n228\t| `extra_body.chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking` | `false` |\n229\t| `models` | The six model IDs and context lengths in [config.ts][config]. |\n230\t\n231\tThe `models` map is written as one value. These writes replace existing\n232\tvalues at the listed keys, including any previous backend selection or\n233\tcustomized Tiiny model map. Other configuration keys are left as they are.\n234\tIf a `hermes config set` call fails, earlier changes remain applied; the\n235\tcommand reports the failure without rolling them back.\n236\t\n237\tThe installer does not select the manager's model or provider, set\n238\t`delegation.provider`, `delegation.base_url`, or\n239\t`delegation.fallback_providers`, download models, or load/unload them.\n240\tThe installer itself does not edit `config.yaml` directly, and it never\n241\tedits `.env`; add `TIINY_API_KEY` yourself as described above. The skill\n242\tis served from the plugin directory, without a separate copy under\n243\t`~/.hermes/skills/`.\n244\t\n245\tA saved `delegation.backend` takes effect from the next Hermes session, not\n246\tthe current one. Restart the gateway or start a new session.\n247\t\n248\t## Check the install\n249\t\n250\t```bash\n251\tnpx hermesrouter doctor\n252\t```\n253\t\n254\t`doctor` prints a pass, warn or fail line for each check: the installed\n255\tdirectory is complete, its version matches the package, no installed file\n256\twas edited, `hermes plugins validate` passes, `delegation.backend` selects\n257\t`tiiny-router`, `python3` is present, and the device answers. It exits\n258\tnon-zero when any check fails. A device that cannot be reached is a\n259\twarning, not a failure.\n260\t\n261\tTo see where a goal would be routed, and to drive the controller, run the\n262\tinstalled scripts through the package:\n263\t\n264\t```bash\n265\tnpx hermesrouter route-check \"index every file in the notes folder\"\n266\tnpx hermesrouter route-check --all\n267\tnpx hermesrouter ctl status\n268\tnpx hermesrouter ctl ensure --model \"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\"\n269\t```\n270\t\n271\t`route-check` and `ctl` run `scripts/route_check.py` and\n272\t`scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` from the installed directory with the system\n273\t`python3`, passing the arguments and the exit code through.\n274\t\n275\t## Upgrade\n276\t\n277\tRun `install` again with the newer package:\n278\t\n279\t```bash\n280\tnpm install -D hermes-tiiny-router@latest\n281\tnpx hermesrouter install\n282\t```\n283\t\n284\t`install` keeps a manifest of what it wrote. If a file in the installed\n285\tdirectory was edited since then, or the directory was not installed by this\n286\tpackage (for example an older copy made by hand), it lists the problem and\n287\tstops. Re-run with `--force` to overwrite.\n288\t\n289\t## Uninstall\n290\t\n291\t```bash\n292\tnpx hermesrouter uninstall\n293\t```\n294\t\n295\tThis removes `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`, and only when its\n296\tmanifest shows this package installed it. It does not change Hermes\n297\tconfig; it prints the `hermes config set` command that unselects the\n298\tbackend.\n299\t\n300\tTo restore ordinary delegation, run this in the same Hermes configuration\n301\tbefore starting another session:\n302\t\n303\t```bash\n304\thermes config set delegation.backend default\n305\t```\n306\t\n307\tUninstall does not restore previous settings or remove `providers.tiiny`.\n308\tAny delegation provider or endpoint you set separately also remains.\n309\t\n310\t## More\n311\t\n312\t- [tiiny-router/SKILL.md](tiiny-router/SKILL.md) -- the procedure the\n313\t  manager agent follows: pick, fit, reserve, load, supervise, verify,\n314\t  release.\n315\t- [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) -- why routing by task shape pays off.\n316\t- [docs/PATTERN.md](docs/PATTERN.md) -- the routing pattern in full.\n317\t- [docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md](docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md) -- the backend, the\n318\t  controller and an end-to-end checklist.\n319\t\n320\t[config]: src/config.ts\n321\t[hermes]: https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/\n322\t[hermes-delegation]: https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/delegation\n323\t[hermes-profiles]: https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/profiles\n324\t[pi]: https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono\n325\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af2d0abd-9e83-4754-8c85-3fb46e7ec1b3","uuid":"a3c9e4f8-8008-4cdf-90ea-b4bd2a31b300","timestamp":"2026-11-22T01:33:22.365Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.install-workflow-fixes-02-config-step-enables-plugin/README.md","content":"# tiiny-router-hermes\n\nTiiny model routing for the Hermes harness.\n\nThis package chooses which model does each job.\nEach specialist model gets the task's goal and context without\ninheriting the manager's full conversation history.\nSee\n[Hermes delegation](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/delegation).\n\nThis installs global config, in `~/.hermes/` -- a Hermes plugin,\ncontroller scripts, and a skill for delegating tasks on\na Tiiny hardware device. (Hermes loads plugins from `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/`.)\n\nWe are using Hermes's pluggable `DelegationProvider` to select\na model, provider, and reasoning settings for each subtask.\n\n\n<details><summary><h2>Contents</h2></summary>\n\n<!-- toc -->\n\n- [Prerequisites](#prerequisites)\n- [Install](#install)\n- [What is the Hermes harness?](#what-is-the-hermes-harness)\n- [Request flow](#request-flow)\n- [When Tiiny routing applies](#when-tiiny-routing-applies)\n- [Reducing model swaps](#reducing-model-swaps)\n- [The config step](#the-config-step)\n  * [Settings written by the installer](#settings-written-by-the-installer)\n- [Check the install](#check-the-install)\n- [Upgrade](#upgrade)\n- [Uninstall](#uninstall)\n- [More](#more)\n\n<!-- tocstop -->\n\n</details>\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n* [Hermes](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/) installed\n* a [tiiny device](https://tiiny.ai/)\n\n## Install\n\nThe npm package is `hermes-tiiny-router`; its command is `hermesrouter`\n(the install command is `npx hermesrouter install`).\n\n```sh\nnpm i -D hermes-tiiny-router\n```\n\nInstall the Hermes plugin, then choose whether to configure it (see\n[the config step](#the-config-step)):\n\n```bash\nnpx hermesrouter install\n```\n\nThis copies a directory to `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`\n(`HERMES_HOME` defaults to `~/.hermes`). It holds the routing backend, the\ncontroller scripts and the skill, which Hermes serves as\n`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`. The installer then runs\n`hermes plugins validate` on the directory.\n\nInstalling the npm dependency alone does not install or configure the\nHermes plugin. **The plugin is installed at the Hermes user level**,\neven when the npm dependency is local to a project.\n\nAdd the device's bearer token to `~/.hermes/.env` yourself.\n\n```sh\n# ~/.hermes/.env\nTIINY_API_KEY=\"...\"\n```\n\n## What is the Hermes harness?\n\n[Hermes Agent][hermes] is a harness from Nous Research. It provides the\nexecution loop, model-provider integration, and session storage, along\nwith persistent memory, reusable skills, scheduled tasks, messaging\nintegrations, and subagent delegation. Its learning features include\nsaving and improving skills and memories across sessions.\n\nThis plugin selects models for subtasks.\n\n## Request flow\n\nWith delegation configured to use Tiiny:\n\n```text\nYour request\n  -> Hermes manager agent\n  -> delegate_task(goal, context)\n  -> Tiiny routing backend\n  -> selected model on the Tiiny device\n  -> result returned to the manager\n```\n\nHermes supplies the child agent's execution loop, tools, and isolated\nconversation. This plugin selects the model, taking the task, the batch\nplan, and the device's loaded models into account. See\n[Hermes delegation][hermes-delegation] for how child agents run and return\ntheir results.\n\n## When Tiiny routing applies\n\nThe intended scope is **Hermes delegating work to Tiiny hardware**. The\nmanager can use a cloud model; it does not need to run on Tiiny. Installing\nthis package does not change how other agent harnesses route tasks.\n\nHermes calls this router for `delegate_task` when its configuration selects\n`delegation.backend: tiiny-router`. That selection persists across new\nsessions using the same configuration. Changing the manager's model or\nprovider does not turn the router on or off.\n\n**The current code does not enforce a Tiiny-only guard.** The skill tells\nthe manager to use it only with Tiiny, but the backend does not validate\nthe delegation provider or endpoint before choosing a Tiiny model and\ncontacting the device. It copies the delegation configuration into the\nreturned route, then sets the model and reasoning overrides. Selecting\nthis backend alone does not bind the child to the `tiiny` provider.\n\nThe installer adds that provider but does not set `delegation.provider`.\nFor Tiiny workers, explicitly select it in the same Hermes configuration:\n\n```bash\nhermes config set delegation.provider tiiny\n```\n\nCheck existing delegation overrides too: `delegation.base_url` takes\nprecedence over the provider. Without a delegation provider or endpoint,\nchildren inherit the manager's provider and credentials. An unreachable\ndevice does not automatically disable this backend, and configured\nfallback providers can send failed child tasks to a cloud model.\n\nUse a dedicated [Hermes profile][hermes-profiles] for Tiiny work, with the\nbackend set to `default` in configurations used for other providers. Set\n`HERMES_HOME` explicitly when installing for a profile so the package and\nits `hermes` subprocesses target the same home. For example, after creating\na profile named `tiiny`:\n\n```bash\nHERMES_HOME=\"$HOME/.hermes/profiles/tiiny\" \\\n  npx hermesrouter install --configure\nHERMES_HOME=\"$HOME/.hermes/profiles/tiiny\" \\\n  hermes config set delegation.provider tiiny\n```\n\nThis separates the configurations; a runtime check would still be needed\nto guarantee that this backend cannot be used with a non-Tiiny route.\n\n## Reducing model swaps\n\nThe package helps avoid repeated loading and unloading in two ways:\n\n- **Reuse loaded models.** For each task, the router first considers its\n  planned model if loaded, then loaded candidates in the task's tier,\n  then the loaded generalist. Without a loaded match, it chooses the\n  tier's default; if residency cannot be read, it uses the generalist\n  unless a plan supplies a model. By default it calls the controller's\n  `ensure_model` before returning the route. An already loaded model is\n  checked and reused rather than reloaded.\n- **Plan model-loading waves.** Given several goals, the controller's\n  `plan` command chooses their models, collects the distinct models,\n  and packs them into waves whose combined NPU share fits within 100%.\n  Models already loaded are packed first. Every task assigned to a\n  particular model gets that model's wave number. A wave can contain\n  several models if they fit together.\n\nFor example, independent goals that would alternate between two models\nthat cannot fit together can instead run all work for one model before\nloading the other. Loading a wave keeps other resident models when there\nis room and skips loading models that are already resident.\n\n**Grouping is planned, but execution depends on the manager following the\nskill.** The router handles one task at a time; it does not maintain a\nqueue or reorder arbitrary `delegate_task` calls. The installed skill\ninstructs the manager to plan the batch, reserve the device, load a wave,\nfinish that wave's work, then load the next. The skill also instructs the\nmanager to run only one generation-heavy child at a time. After the batch,\n`release` restores the controller's required models and clears the plan\nand lock; restoration can itself require loading models.\n\nAd hoc delegation still gets model selection and on-demand loading, but\ndoes not get automatic grouping across separate calls. Batching reduces\nswaps when the work permits it; it does not eliminate their time cost.\nSee the [routing skill](tiiny-router/SKILL.md) for the full procedure.\n\n## The config step\n\n`npx hermesrouter install` copies the plugin and validates it, then offers\nto change Hermes configuration through `hermes config set`.\n\n```bash\nnpx hermesrouter install                 # prompts in a terminal\nnpx hermesrouter install --configure     # applies without asking\nnpx hermesrouter install --no-configure  # installs files only\n```\n\nWithout a terminal and without either flag, it skips configuration and\nprints the commands. Declining the prompt or using `--no-configure` also\nleaves settings unchanged.\n\nThese are persistent Hermes user settings, not settings in the npm\nproject. With the default Hermes home/profile they live in\n`~/.hermes/config.yaml`; a named profile has its own configuration. The\ninstaller copies files to `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/` (falling\nback to `~/.hermes`) and lets the invoked `hermes` command choose its\nconfiguration. Use an explicit `HERMES_HOME` to keep those targets aligned\nwhen working with profiles.\n\n### Settings written by the installer\n\nThe config step sets `delegation.backend` to `tiiny-router` and writes the\nfollowing fields under `providers.tiiny`:\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| `name` | `tiiny` |\n| `api` | `http://openai.api.tiiny/v1` |\n| `key_env` | `TIINY_API_KEY` |\n| `transport` | `chat_completions` |\n| `default_model` | `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` |\n| `context_length` | `262144` |\n| `models_discovered` | `false` |\n| `extra_body.chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking` | `false` |\n| `models` | The six model IDs and context lengths in [config.ts][config]. |\n\nThe `models` map is written as one value. These writes replace existing\nvalues at the listed keys, including any previous backend selection or\ncustomized Tiiny model map. Other configuration keys are left as they are.\nIf a `hermes config set` call fails, earlier changes remain applied; the\ncommand reports the failure without rolling them back.\n\nThe installer does not select the manager's model or provider, set\n`delegation.provider`, `delegation.base_url`, or\n`delegation.fallback_providers`, download models, or load/unload them.\nThe installer itself does not edit `config.yaml` directly, and it never\nedits `.env`; add `TIINY_API_KEY` yourself as described above. The skill\nis served from the plugin directory, without a separate copy under\n`~/.hermes/skills/`.\n\nA saved `delegation.backend` takes effect from the next Hermes session, not\nthe current one. Restart the gateway or start a new session.\n\n## Check the install\n\n```bash\nnpx hermesrouter doctor\n```\n\n`doctor` prints a pass, warn or fail line for each check: the installed\ndirectory is complete, its version matches the package, no installed file\nwas edited, `hermes plugins validate` passes, `delegation.backend` selects\n`tiiny-router`, `python3` is present, and the device answers. It exits\nnon-zero when any check fails. A device that cannot be reached is a\nwarning, not a failure.\n\nTo see where a goal would be routed, and to drive the controller, run the\ninstalled scripts through the package:\n\n```bash\nnpx hermesrouter route-check \"index every file in the notes folder\"\nnpx hermesrouter route-check --all\nnpx hermesrouter ctl status\nnpx hermesrouter ctl ensure --model \"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\"\n```\n\n`route-check` and `ctl` run `scripts/route_check.py` and\n`scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` from the installed directory with the system\n`python3`, passing the arguments and the exit code through.\n\n## Upgrade\n\nRun `install` again with the newer package:\n\n```bash\nnpm install -D hermes-tiiny-router@latest\nnpx hermesrouter install\n```\n\n`install` keeps a manifest of what it wrote. If a file in the installed\ndirectory was edited since then, or the directory was not installed by this\npackage (for example an older copy made by hand), it lists the problem and\nstops. Re-run with `--force` to overwrite.\n\n## Uninstall\n\n```bash\nnpx hermesrouter uninstall\n```\n\nThis removes `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`, and only when its\nmanifest shows this package installed it. It does not change Hermes\nconfig; it prints the `hermes config set` command that unselects the\nbackend.\n\nTo restore ordinary delegation, run this in the same Hermes configuration\nbefore starting another session:\n\n```bash\nhermes config set delegation.backend default\n```\n\nUninstall does not restore previous settings or remove `providers.tiiny`.\nAny delegation provider or endpoint you set separately also remains.\n\n## More\n\n- [tiiny-router/SKILL.md](tiiny-router/SKILL.md) -- the procedure the\n  manager agent follows: pick, fit, reserve, load, supervise, verify,\n  release.\n- [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) -- why routing by task shape pays off.\n- [docs/PATTERN.md](docs/PATTERN.md) -- the routing pattern in full.\n- [docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md](docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md) -- the backend, the\n  controller and an end-to-end checklist.\n\n[config]: src/config.ts\n[hermes]: https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/\n[hermes-delegation]: https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/delegation\n[hermes-profiles]: https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/profiles\n[pi]: https://github.com/badlogic/pi-mono\n","numLines":325,"startLine":1,"totalLines":325}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XwaEyU5c4nBjGpNX3xVue1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
