{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChH7AYNxRx3LasB8cYaHN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the remaining checklist items:\n- [ ] Checked by hand under a Python `pty.fork()` that the enable step does not block an interactive install on a consent prompt\n- [ ] Each new guard test is checked to go red by briefly breaking the code (restore from a copy, not `git checkout`)\n\nThe red-check for the main test was already done above. Let me also verify the `--no-configure` guard goes red with a temporary change, and verify the pty check.\n\nFor the pty check, I need to simulate what `hermes plugins enable` would do in an interactive terminal. The concern is that Hermes might prompt for consent (`_enable_consent`). Since our fake hermes doesn't prompt, I need to do a manual-ish check with a real pty. Let me write a quick Python script."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":78886,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":347},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"af2d0abd-9e83-4754-8c85-3fb46e7ec1b3","uuid":"b90ee869-e496-42a8-8536-5ecf276c04e4","timestamp":"2026-11-22T01:34:49.469Z","request_id":"req_011ChH7AYD3i2V6f7Xmtgw7v"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011ChH7AYNxRx3LasB8cYaHN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Uo5bRFyxVbWhB6YzsA3Tnr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -B -c '\nimport pty, os, sys, time, select\n\npid, fd = pty.fork()\nif pid == 0:\n    # Child: run install --configure\n    os.environ[\"HERMES_HOME\"] = \"/tmp/pty-test-hermes\"\n    os.environ[\"TIINY_API_KEY\"] = \"test\"\n    os.environ[\"TIINY_BASE_URL\"] = \"http://127.0.0.1:9/v1\"\n    os.environ[\"TIINY_HOST\"] = \"http://127.0.0.1:9\"\n    os.execvp(\"node\", [\"node\", \"dist/cli.js\", \"install\", \"--configure\"])\nelse:\n    # Parent: read output, timeout after 10s\n    output = b\"\"\n    deadline = time.time() + 10\n    while time.time() < deadline:\n        r, _, _ = select.select([fd], [], [], 1.0)\n        if r:\n            try:\n                chunk = os.read(fd, 4096)\n                if not chunk:\n                    break\n                output += chunk\n            except OSError:\n                break\n    # Check if still running (blocked on input)\n    import signal\n    try:\n        result = os.waitpid(pid, os.WNOHANG)\n        if result == (0, 0):\n            print(\"BLOCKED: process still running after 10s\")\n            os.kill(pid, signal.SIGTERM)\n            os.waitpid(pid, 0)\n            sys.exit(1)\n        else:\n            code = os.waitstatus_to_exitcode(result[1])\n            print(f\"Exited with code {code} (not blocked)\")\n    except ChildProcessError:\n        print(\"Process already exited (not blocked)\")\n    print(\"Output:\", output.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")[:500])\n' 2>&1","description":"PTY check that enable step does not block","timeout":20000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":78886,"cache_creation":{"e